            <ArticleTitle>Enhanced long-term stability of perovskite solar cells by 3-hydroxypyridine dipping.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1829-1831</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09492a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lead halide perovskite solar cells show poor stability due to their ionic material character. Here, we introduce a dipping method to modify the perovskite layer with 3-hydroxypyridine molecules. The long-term stability of solar cells is greatly enhanced and shows no obvious decay after 90 hour steady-state measurements.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
